# No trailing slash, deliberately.
#
# `node_modules/` matches a directory and NOT a symlink, and this repo had a symlink here — an
# absolute path into one developer's home directory, pointing at itself, committed. On that machine
# it happened to resolve; anywhere else it dangles. What it cost was silent: `npm run build` ran
# `tsc` (which passed), then `vite`, which could not resolve through the loop and did nothing, and
# the whole thing still exited 0. The dist/ bundle simply stopped changing while every source edit
# looked applied.
node_modules
*.local

# The marketplace root ignores *.png, but dist/ is committed on purpose so that
# `/plugin install` never needs an npm install — and a PWA with no icons is not
# installable. These three are generated by build-pwa.mjs, not pasted in.
!dist/icons/*.png
